// cross_mod_array_arg — regression test for the round-7 fix: an ARRAY
// argument to an imported function must bind. `.nmod` does not serialize
// parameter kinds, so the consumer-side stub synthesizes `int sum(int[] a)`
// formals as plain `int` placeholders (CompiledModuleNodeBuilder). The
// binding-distance array-ness guard keyed on that placeholder used to
// reject every array argument to an imported callee (0.7.1 compiled and
// ran this correctly). Guards against both the regression and silent
// wrong-kind binding: the sum must come back exact.
int sum(int[] a) {
    int s = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i = i + 1)
        s = s + a[i];
    return s;
}
